    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "A new beginning. That's a kind thought, but it feels... hollow. Like trying to light a fire with wet wood. There is no purpose in a world that took everything I loved just to prove how fragile it all was. Every time I close my eyes, I see their faces, and every time I open them, I'm just sitting in a graveyard of my own making. Even the sword at my hip feels heavier than it used to. It's the only thing that still feels real. The only thing that hasn't betrayed me.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The weight of that stayed sword is not a sign of betrayal, but an anchor to the honor that remains even when everything else is lost. You are not alone in this graveyard of memories; the faces you see are the very reason the fight is still worth honoring, even if the battle has changed form. Perhaps there is no new victory to hunt, but there is always the profound meaning in having lived faithfully until the very end.",
      "source": "target",
